findings.recommendation:
HTML-escape the token before substitution, or assert that the token matches the expected base64url pattern (^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$) before sending. Preferred fix: apply htmlEscape to all dynamic values in buildBody, not only {NAME}. Example:

private String buildBody(String templatePath, String name, Map<String,String> extraVars) {
    String body = loadTemplate(templatePath).replace("{NAME}", htmlEscape(name));
    for (var entry : extraVars.entrySet()) {
        body = body.replace(entry.getKey(), htmlEscape(entry.getValue()));
    }
    return body;
}

Alternatively, validate token format with Objects.requireNonNull + a regex check at service entry points.

Add single-quote escaping:

static String htmlEscape(String input) {
    return input
        .replace("&", "&amp;")
        .replace("<", "&lt;")
        .replace(">", "&gt;")
        .replace("\"", "&quot;")
        .replace("'", "&#39;");
}

HTML-escape all dynamic values before substitution, including supportEmail:

public void sendAccountBlockedEmail(String to, String name, String supportEmail) {
